Name:           discord-game-presence
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        @RELEASE@%{?dist}
Summary:        Rich Presence for games and apps Discord ignores on Linux

License:        MIT
URL:            https://github.com/gabrielmf1998/Discord-Arrpc-Detector-KDE
Source0:        %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz

BuildArch:      noarch
Requires:       python3
Requires:       python3-gobject
Requires:       gtk3
Requires:       iproute
Recommends:     libappindicator-gtk3
Recommends:     librsvg2

%description
Discord only detects games listed with a Windows or macOS executable, so
native Linux games, anything running under Proton and media apps are never
picked up. This daemon watches the processes itself and speaks Discord's IPC
protocol directly, publishing the presence.

A GTK3 tray icon (no Qt, no windows) controls which apps Discord can see, the
icon look, and autostart.

%prep
%setup -q -c

%build

%install
cp -a usr %{buildroot}/

%files
%{_bindir}/discord-game-presence
%{_bindir}/discord-presence-tray
%{_userunitdir}/discord-game-presence.service
%{_userunitdir}/discord-game-presence-tray.service
%{_datadir}/applications/discord-presence-tray.desktop
%{_datadir}/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/discord-game-presence.svg
%doc %{_datadir}/doc/discord-game-presence/README.md
%doc %{_datadir}/doc/discord-game-presence/INSTALAR.txt
%doc %{_datadir}/doc/discord-game-presence/config.exemplo.json

%post
cat <<'NOTE'

Discord Presence installed. Enable it for your user (no root):
    systemctl --user enable --now discord-game-presence.service
    systemctl --user enable --now discord-game-presence-tray.service
NOTE

%changelog
* Sat Aug 29 2026 kxinha <gabriel17166@gmail.com> - @VERSION@-@RELEASE@
- First packaged release: daemon plus GTK3 tray icon.
